      "math_academy_id": "q-213188",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Let $A={3,6,8}$ and $B={1,4,7}$ Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R={(x,y)\\in A\\times B\\,:\\,x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)}?$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set is plotted along the horizontal axis,\n\n- the second set is plotted along the vertical axis, and\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).$\n\n- If $x=3,$ then the values $y=1,7$ satisfy $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(3,1)$ and $(3,7),$ and we should plot these points on the graph.\n\n- If $x=6,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(6,4),$ and we should plot this point on the graph.\n\n- If $x=8,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2).$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(8,4),$ and we should plot this point on the graph.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120255/assets/42f68f95fe216faacbfaa051ec0a1a6cf75fe7e4598061e94f2ec6be87f9541f.png)",
